  "notes": "West leads the ♠7 against 3NT. South appears to have at least 10 tricks (2 or 3 in spades, the ♥A, 6 diamond tricks, and the ♣A). The blockage in the diamond suit could spell trouble if that suit is 4-1.\n\nIn order to cater to this possibility, South must win the ♠A at trick 1. South cashes his ♦A and ♦Q. South then gives up a trick to the ♠K. South can win any return and reach dummy's diamond suit with the newly created spade entry.\n\nIf South had won the first trick in dummy, the above position would result after South unblocks the diamonds. South would have no way to get to dummy's remaining diamonds and the contract would fail.",
